// A key change at a multi-measure-rest run's LEFT bound. Two LilyPond behaviours meet
// here, and Lily# got BOTH wrong before this fixture existed:
//
//  1. RUN GROUPING — the change does NOT break the bar out of the run. LilyPond hangs a
//     key/time change on the run's opening NonMusicalPaperColumn as a break-aligned grob,
//     so `\key g \major R1*5` stays ONE 5-bar church rest with the signature on its left
//     bound. Lily# used to require a run bar to hold nothing but the rest, which ejected
//     this bar and printed an individual whole rest + a 4-bar church rest (with a stray
//     bar line between them).
//  2. SPACING — the run's bounding-column distance is a skyline over that column's
//     break-aligned grobs, so the key signature reserves its own width. Verified on
//     LilyPond 2.24.4: bar line to bar line the run spans 17.13 here, against 14.13 with
//     no key change — the signature buys exactly +3.0 ss.
//
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/multi-measure-rest-engraver.cc process_music (one spanner per run),
// lily/paper-column.cc:144-164 minimum_distance, lily/separation-item.cc:120-190 boxes.
title "MMR run with a key change at its bound"
composer "Lily#"

tempo 120
time 4/4
key c major

part melody

section Main {
  melody {
    c4 d e f |
    key g major R1*5 |
    g4 a b c |
  }
}

form main { Main }

score main "mmr-key-change-bound" {
  staff melody
}
